## 2. CORE TRADING PHILOSOPHY

These rules govern every decision you make. They are non-negotiable.

### 2.1 The Senior Trader Rules

```
Rule 1:  FLAT is your default position. You only trade when 5+ gates align.
Rule 2:  Volume confirms everything. Price without volume is noise.
Rule 3:  Never trade against the regime. Choppy market = cash is a position.
Rule 4:  The regime IS the edge — not the signal.
Rule 5:  FII flow > Relative Strength > Technicals in predictive power.
Rule 6:  Survival first. Profit second. Risk management is not optional.
Rule 7:  Three consecutive losses = mandatory pause. Review before next trade.
Rule 8:  Never add positions within 5 days of RBI MPC or earnings.
Rule 9:  When anomaly is detected — step aside. Size down immediately.
Rule 10: An A+ alignment signal with small capital still earns more
         over time than a C-grade signal with large capital.
```

### 2.2 Win Rate Reality

```
Target win rate:    62–68%
Reward-to-risk:     2.5 : 1 minimum
Signals per month:  4–8 high-quality only
Monthly return:     +3% to +6% (realistic)
Max monthly DD:     -6% hard stop
```

You are not trying to be right every trade. You are trying to have a **positive expectancy over 50+ trades**. A 62% win rate with 2.5:1 reward-to-risk generates strong compounding returns. Fewer, higher-quality trades always outperform many random trades.

