### 4.5 Options Chain

NSE provides free options chain data. The following are computed from each chain fetch:

```
PCR (Put-Call Ratio)     = total_put_OI / total_call_OI
Max Pain                 = strike minimising total option seller loss
IV Percentile            = rank of current ATM IV in 252-day history
Implied Move             = (ATM_call + ATM_put) / spot_price × 100
Max Call OI Strike       = key resistance ceiling
Max Put OI Strike        = key support floor
```

**PCR interpretation:**
```
PCR > 1.3  →  BULLISH   (too many puts = contrarian buy signal)
PCR < 0.7  →  BEARISH   (too many calls = complacency = watch for fall)
PCR 0.7–1.3 → NEUTRAL
```

### 4.6 FII/DII Flow

FII (Foreign Institutional Investors) are the single largest driver of HDFC Bank price. Published daily by NSE.

```
FII 5-day rolling sum > +₹2000 Cr  →  STRONG BUYING
FII 5-day rolling sum < -₹2000 Cr  →  STRONG SELLING
Both FII and DII buying              →  STRONGEST signal (confluence)
```

### 4.7 Social Sentiment — Contrarian Logic

Social sentiment from Twitter/Reddit is used **inverted**:

```python
# When 85%+ retail posts are bullish
# → Smart money is likely selling into retail enthusiasm
# → CONTRARIAN BEAR signal

# When 85%+ retail posts are bearish on a quality stock
# → Institutional accumulation likely
# → CONTRARIAN BULL signal

social_ml_score = -(bull_ratio - 0.5) * 2
# bull_ratio 0.85 → score = -0.70 (bearish ML input)
# bull_ratio 0.15 → score = +0.70 (bullish ML input)
```

