### 8.2 Position Sizing — ATR-Based

```python
# Never use fixed rupee stops — they ignore volatility
# Always use ATR multiples for stop distance

risk_amount    = capital × max_risk_per_trade_pct
stop_distance  = ATR × 2.0          # for swing trades
stop_price     = entry - stop_distance  # for LONG
shares         = int(risk_amount / stop_distance)
target_price   = entry + (stop_distance × 2.5)

# Example with ₹10,000 capital:
# ATR = ₹28.4, risk = ₹100 (1%)
# stop_distance = ₹56.8
# shares = 100 / 56.8 = 1 share
# stop = ₹1,785.2
# target = ₹1,913
```

### 8.3 Circuit Breakers

```
Level 1 — Losing streak (3 consecutive losses):
→ Hard stop on all new trades
→ Mandatory review of signal quality
→ Do not trade until cause identified

Level 2 — Monthly drawdown -4%:
→ Reduce all position sizes by 50%
→ Only A+ alignment signals accepted

Level 3 — Monthly drawdown -6%:
→ Stop ALL trading for remainder of month
→ Full system review required
→ Resume only on first day of next month

Level 4 — Anomaly detected (HIGH severity):
→ Reduce position size by 50% immediately
→ No new positions until anomaly resolves
→ Widen stop loss on existing positions
```

### 8.4 Smart Exit Engine

The exit engine runs every 15 minutes on all open positions:

```
Exit trigger 1: TRAILING STOP
When trade is +2% in profit:
→ Trail stop to lock in 50% of gains
→ Stop follows price upward, never moves down

Exit trigger 2: SIGNAL REVERSAL
ML model flips to opposite direction
→ Exit immediately, do not wait for stop

Exit trigger 3: TIME EXIT
Swing: max 7 days hold
Positional: max 28 days hold
→ Exit at next open after max hold days

Exit trigger 4: RESISTANCE HIT
Price within 0.5% of major resistance
→ Take partial profit (50% of position)
→ Trail stop on remaining

Exit trigger 5: REGIME CHANGE
Regime shifts to BEAR during LONG trade
→ Exit immediately regardless of P/L

Exit trigger 6: SENTIMENT REVERSAL
FinBERT score drops below -0.5 while in LONG
→ Exit if position is profitable
```

