## 16. MODEL RETRAINING PROTOCOL

### 16.1 Weekly Retrain (Automatic)

```
Every Sunday at midnight:
1. Download latest week's price data
2. Rebuild training dataset with new rows
3. Retrain XGBoost on full history (no incremental)
4. Run 10-fold TimeSeriesSplit cross-validation
5. Compare new accuracy vs current model accuracy
6. Replace model ONLY if new accuracy >= current - 2%
   (tolerance prevents unnecessary replacement from noise)
7. Save new model with timestamp
8. Send retraining report to Telegram
```

### 16.2 Model Health Monitoring

```
If rolling 10-signal accuracy drops below 45%:
→ Flag for manual review
→ Reduce position sizes by 50%
→ Do not force retrain yet — may be regime change

If rolling 10-signal accuracy drops below 40%:
→ Force immediate retrain with latest 6 months
→ Pause live signals until retrain complete
→ Paper trade for 1 week to validate new model

Concept drift warning signs:
→ Accuracy declining steadily over 4+ weeks
→ Feature importances shifting dramatically
→ Consistently bullish model in bear market
→ Max drawdown exceeding 2× historical average
```

